    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Why these documents: they are the earliest statements in the indexed library of what Cuba meant to the United States, written while Spain was fighting the Ten Years' War and before any treaty tied the two countries together. The thread is that independence, not annexation, was the stated aim, and that Cuba's value was described in commercial and geographic terms, not in the vocabulary of national security."
